.TH BRIX-CONFIG-MIGRATE 1 "2026-10-12" "BriX-Cache 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brix-config-migrate \- suggest a BriX-Cache configuration from XRootD input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brix-config-migrate
.RI [ options ] " xrootd.cfg"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brix-config-migrate
is an offline migration assistant.  It parses one XRootD configuration file
and writes a suggested nginx configuration using BriX-Cache directives.
It recognizes common POSIX, PSS/PFC, XrdCeph/librados, GSI/VOMS, XrdAcc,
TLS, CMS, TPC, and XrdHttp settings.
.PP
The output is a suggestion, not a semantic guarantee.  Ambiguous or unsupported
input is preserved as
.B REVIEW
comments and in the optional JSON report.  The tool does not open include
files, load plugins, expand environment variables, or contact origins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " FILE
Write the suggested nginx configuration to FILE instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-report " " FILE
Write the per-directive conversion decisions as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit with status 3 when any review or unsupported item remains.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca-bundle " " PATH
Supply the BriX trusted-CA bundle where the source only identifies a CA
directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-authdb-input " " FILE
Read this explicitly named XrdAcc authdb companion.  The source configuration's
authdb path is never followed automatically.
.TP
.BR \-\-authdb-output " " FILE
Write the BriX-compatible XrdAcc authdb and point the generated configuration
at FILE.  Must be used with
.BR \-\-authdb-input .
.TP
.BR \-\-vomsdir " " PATH
Override the VOMS trust directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-voms-cert-dir " " PATH
Set the VOMS issuer-certificate directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-require-vo " " PATH=VO
Add a path-scoped VO requirement.  May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-ceph-pool " " NAME
Supply the librados pool when it cannot be inferred safely.
.TP
.BR \-\-ceph-conf " " PATH
Supply the Ceph configuration path.
.TP
.BR \-\-ceph-key-prefix " " PREFIX
Supply the object-key prefix for the librados backend.
.TP
.BR \-\-n2n-scheme " " SCHEME
Select an explicit name-to-name mapping: identity, ral, or cephfs_path.
.TP
.BR \-\-n2n-pool " " NAME
Supply the name-to-name pool.
.TP
.BR \-\-n2n-prefix " " PREFIX
Supply the name-to-name path prefix.
.TP
.BR \-\-http-port " " PORT
Select the WebDAV port. When XrdHttp and root share a source port, this is a
private loopback listener behind
.BR brix_http_handoff ;
when omitted, the next numeric port is used.
.TP
.BR \-\-http-connect-timeout " " TIME
Set the private WebDAV connection deadline emitted for a shared source port.
The default is 5s.
.TP
.BR \-\-http-idle-timeout " " TIME
Set the per-direction idle deadline emitted for an HTTP handoff. The default
is 75s.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for a conversion (including review items without
.BR \-\-strict ),
2 for invalid input or an I/O error, and 3 for unresolved review items in
strict mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
brix-config-migrate --strict --report decisions.json xrootd.cfg > nginx.conf
brix-config-migrate --authdb-input authdb --authdb-output brix-authdb xrootd.cfg
brix-config-migrate --ceph-pool atlas --n2n-scheme cephfs_path xrootd-ceph.cfg
nginx -t -c "$PWD/nginx.conf"
.EE
.SH SECURITY
Input is treated strictly as data.  Includes and plugin paths are never
followed or executed.  Generated arguments are nginx-quoted.  Always inspect
every REVIEW item and validate the result with
.BR nginx (8)
before deployment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8)
